cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MathHead in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MathHead: a deterministic mathematics engine with an honesty contract"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Çakır"
    given-names: "Tanzer"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
repository-code: "https://github.com/tanzercakir-commits/MathHead"
abstract: >-
  A verification and discovery engine for finite mathematics: an LCF-style proof kernel with a fully
  derived trust base, counterexample-first refutation at nauty scale, pure-integer spectral
  certificates, SAT-bracketed Ramsey numbers with independently re-verified witnesses, live hunts on
  open conjectures, and Lean 4 export. Every verdict carries an explicit epistemic tier.
keywords: [automated-reasoning, combinatorics, graph-theory, SAT, proof-kernel, conjecture-checking]
license: MIT
